<article class="env-lemma" id="03AW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03AW">Lemma <span data-tag="03AW">21.10.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{U} = \{ U_ i \to U\} _{i \in I}$ be a covering of $\mathcal{C}$. Let $\mathcal{I}$ be an injective abelian sheaf, i.e., an injective object of $\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C})$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \check{H}^ p(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{I}) = \left\{  \begin{matrix}  \mathcal{I}(U) 

&  \text{if} 

&  p = 0 

\\  0 

&  \text{if} 

&  p > 0 

\end{matrix} \right.  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/03F6" data-tag="03F6">21.10.1</a> we see that $\mathcal{I}$ is an injective object in $\textit{PAb}(\mathcal{C})$. Hence we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/03AU" data-tag="03AU">21.9.6</a> (or its proof) to see the vanishing of higher Čech cohomology group. For the zeroth see Lemma <a href="/tag/03AN" data-tag="03AN">21.8.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>